        "font" : "CMR10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "This means that for given angle ω one gets the corresponding exponents λ ∈ C by solving (separately) the two transcendental, scalar equations sinλω = ±λsinω. All values Reλ ∈ [21,4] are given for ωk = kπ/10, k = 4,5,...,20, in [Dau89]."
